  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 02 at 13 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy with needle localization  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented breast specimen  A short stitch designates superior and long stitch designates medial  The anterior half is inked black  the posterior half inked blue  the medial edge is inked yellow and the lateral edge inked red  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to superior inferior axis  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm mass 0 2cm away from the posterior margin  0 7cm from the anterior margin and 2 5cm away from the medial margin  The mass is rimmed by a thin irregular area of white  rubbery fibrotic tissue  There is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white  hardened well defined area abutting the medial and anterior margins and 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is fibrofatty with no masses identified  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes A I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm lymph node  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a yellow  hemorrhagic cut surface  All submitted in cassette J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shave  are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes K L  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  