Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  Positive for carcinoma on biopsy approximately one month ago                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    RESIDUAL INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA WITH METASTASES TO THREE OF EIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE     CYSTIC CAVITY  ACUTE INFLAMMATION AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FIBROSIS AND MULTINUCLEATED FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE    SKIN SCAR  NOTE  Carcinoma extends to within 0 5cm of the deep inked resection margin which is the closest resection margin  One lymph node has extracapsular extension of carcinoma into perinodal adipose tissue  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 30                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy  measuring 25 x 20 x 4 5cm  partially covered by a 14 x 5 5cm skin ellipse  Two sutures are present on the skin ellipse designating the superior and lateral aspect of the specimen  A 3 2cm incision that is partially healed and contains several black sutures is present inferolaterally to an unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal in the region of the previous incision a stellate shaped 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm firm  gray white area with an adjacent 1 x 0 5cm blood filled cystic cavity and fat necrosis  This firm area extends to within 0 1cm from the deep inked resection margin  which is the closest resection margin  The axillary adipose tissue is sectioned and reveals several tan pink  soft and grossly unremarkable lymph nodes and one firm  gray white node  measuring 0 6cm in diameter  Section Code A C   tumor and inked deep resection margin D H   additional resection of tumor I J   unremarkable breast parenchyma K   nipple L   skin scar M O   axillary lymph nodes Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID TYPE WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS AND CANCERISATION OF LOBULES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is only present on 2 slides out of 8  measures 0 3cm in diameter extending to within 0 1cm from an inked margin  The intraductal component is present on 3 slides out of 8 and does not involve margins  All the tissue was submitted for microscopic examination  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 0 6cm fragment of breast tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibroadipose cut surface with focally hemorrhagic areas  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm nodule which corresponds to the microcalcification on mammogram  The suspicious nodule is submitted in cassette A  and the remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes B through H  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS   FIRM LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Absent.
