ents are dissected out of the lateral end of the specimen  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Cassettes K  L and M each contains three whole nodules  Two whole nodules are submitted in cassette N  Cassettes O and P  each contain five whole nodules and cassette Q contains three whole nodules  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary tissue   are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The larger fibroadipose nodule is dissected to reveal two nodular soft tissues  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each nodule is bisected and submitted individually in cassettes S and T  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION , Absent.
