Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE LATERAL AND ANTERIOR MARGINS   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  RADIAL SCARS  MICROSCOPIC  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION   INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCALLY ATYPICAL  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Seven specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm incision of breast biopsy with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Inferior is yellow  superior is red  lateral is blue  medial is green  anterior and posterior are black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate gritty mass present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  Mass is submitted in cassettes A through C with anterior  black   lateral  blue   and posterior  black overinked in yellow   Needle localization site  slightly firm no gross tumor  and anterior margin are submitted in D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are the 6 remaining specimens  Labeled as  left breast  additional anterior medial margin  is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal fibrocystic changes  submitted entirely in cassettes E through J  Labeled as  left breast  final shaved margins  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  They are inked and sectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue with focal cystic changes  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes K  L and M  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  submitted in N through S  Labeled as  reexcision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing a 4 8cm well healed  linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in blue  while the inferior aspect is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with an associated area of stellate fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and extending to the superior and inferior margins  Posterior to the biopsy cavity is a rubbery  tan white  nodular mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and present at superior  inferior and posterior margins  The biopsy cavity itself is 0 2cm from the nearest  inferior  margin  Section code  T W  Biopsy cavity  nearest margin in W  lateral to medial X Y  Adjacent fibrous areas Z  Uninvolved parenchyma Designated right axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension and submitted in cassettes AA through DD  Labeled as  additional axillary tissue  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension submitted entirely in cassette EE  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EZXCIS PART G  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION   report_end  , Absent.
