stitch designating the inferior  and a long black stitch the medial margins  A localization wire is received separate in the specimen container  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm poorly delineated indurated grey white to tan pink area with surrounding hemorrhage which comes to 0 2cm of the anterior  0 5cm of the medial  0 8cm of the lateral  1 7cm of the posterior  1 5cm of the superior  and 2 2cm of the inferior margins  An S shaped silver metal clip is noted along the mid postero lateral aspect of the specimen  The remaining cut surface shows dense  focally nodular grey white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted from inferior to superior as D J  with the lesion in E I  and the tissue bearing the the S shaped clip as H and BB  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right deep  are 2 fibroadipose soft tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  There is a stitch on one end of each specimen  This end is inked black  and the smaller fragments entirely submitted in cassettes K L and the larger one in cassettes M N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface which is smooth  The outer surface is roughened and focally hemorrhagic  The stitch surface is inked black  and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes O P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm soft tissue  The white  smooth surface is stitched and the under side is focally hemorrhagic and more roughened  The stitch surface is inked black  and the specimen is entirely submitted in c